{"id": 28, "ts": 1780600597.0125978, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s thorough endorsement of Candidate\u202fC, and I still see C as the strongest overall fit given the solid evidence of 100\u202f% reliability, calmness under pressure, quick correct decisions, and a positive crew atmosphere. However, the lack of any data on C\u2019s technical depth\u2014beyond the general note that he makes correct decisions quickly\u2014leaves a gap in assessing his ability to manage the complex systems of long\u2011distance flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB, while noted as uncooperative and grumpy, has clear evidence of strong technical competence (excellent computer skills, good weather assessment) and proven stress resilience. Since I have now confirmed that we have no information on B\u2019s adaptability or feedback orientation, we cannot weigh those positively or negatively. If we can establish that Candidate\u202fA or D brings comparable reliability and crew\u2011cooperation with stronger technical competence, they might become viable alternatives. For now, I maintain my provisional vote for **Candidate\u202fC**, but I recommend we gather any missing technical competence evidence for C (or comparable data for A and D) before finalizing."}
