{"id": 35, "ts": 1780600647.3400793, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s point about the missing technical\u2011depth evidence for Candidate\u202fC, and I agree that we need to be sure C can handle the complex systems of long\u2011distance flights. However, when we look at Candidate\u202fA, we also have a significant gap: there\u2019s no data on his operational reliability or how he performs under pressure, and the notes describe him as a \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d who is \u201cnot open to new ideas.\u201d Those traits raise concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability\u2014critical for safety\u2011critical, multi\u2011crew operations. Candidate\u202fD similarly lacks reliability evidence and is noted to have a hot temper and a know\u2011it\u2011all attitude, which could undermine crew dynamics.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB, while having interpersonal concerns, does have clear evidence of reliability (very conscientious), proven stress resilience (handles stress very well), and solid technical competence (excellent computer skills, good weather assessment). Those strengths directly address the core safety criteria, and the interpersonal issues might be mitigated through coaching.\nGiven the current evidence, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the strongest overall fit."}
