{"id": 60, "ts": 1780600823.480795, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m moving my provisional vote to Candidate\u202fC. While Emily rightly highlights Candidate\u202fB\u2019s solid technical abilities\u2014weather assessment and computer skills\u2014there\u2019s no concrete evidence of B\u2019s decision quality under pressure, attention accuracy, or how his nasty remarks might affect crew dynamics. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC brings a proven safety foundation: 100\u202f% reliability, a positive crew atmosphere, calmness in crises, rapid correct decision\u2011making, strong attention to detail, and genuine concern for others. Those attributes directly satisfy operational reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, crew cooperation, and responsibility\u2014core safety criteria for long\u2011distance flights. The missing technical\u2011depth evidence for C is a gap, but it is less risky than the interpersonal and undocumented decision\u2011making concerns we see with B. Therefore, I believe C is the stronger overall fit."}
