{"id": 93, "ts": 1780601020.531906, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I agree with James and Emily that we still lack concrete evidence on the two remaining critical gaps: Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision\u2011quality under pressure, attention\u2011accuracy performance, and adaptability, and Candidate\u202fC\u2019s willingness to accept feedback or pursue further education. James confirmed there are no specific examples demonstrating B\u2019s decision\u2011making or attention in high\u2011stress situations, and Emily has no additional observations beyond C\u2019s limited appetite for further education. Without that evidence, B\u2019s strong points (conscientiousness, stress handling, weather assessment, computer skills) cannot outweigh the safety\u2011critical strengths we already have for C\u2014100\u202f% reliability, calmness, rapid correct decisions, strong attention, and a positive crew atmosphere. The only remaining concern for C is a modest openness to further learning, which is less hazardous than B\u2019s documented uncooperative and grumpy behavior that could erode cockpit cohesion. Therefore, I keep my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
